    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d927">

                <pb facs="0865" n="761" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg761"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6574.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-09T12:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 9, 1913—noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>96. The Department’s March 8, 6 p.m. Hostetter’s telegram was handed in substance
                    to this Government. I have been sending to the President and the Minister of War
                    every day the substance of all consular telegrams which seemed of value to the
                    Government in restoring order. The Department’s telegram precisely reflects my
                    views and I have been following a policy identical therewith.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
